      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_b2a795af",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: bitch_please_i_m_native_american; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The image features a historical photograph of a Native American man, overlaid with the text 'bitch please i'm native american.' The overall intent is to use the image of a dignified, traditionally dressed Native American to assert a claim of superiority or to dismiss criticism by invoking identity as a shield. This is a hateful meme because it weaponizes identity to deflect or mock, potentially targeting Native Americans by reducing their complex cultural and historical experiences to a simplistic, performative statement. The tone is confrontational and dismissive, and the use of the word 'bitch' combined with the assertion of Native identity is intended to provoke or belittle, which constitutes a direct attack based on ethnicity. The meme does not promote understanding or respect but rather uses the image of a respected figure to justify a hostile or dismissive stance, which is inherently harmful and hateful.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_00e42518"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
