      "label": "Historical representation of Native Americans in media and popular culture",
      "description": "The image is a historical photograph, and its use in a meme relies on the real-world understanding that such images are often appropriated or recontextualized to serve contemporary, often offensive, narratives. The dignified portrayal of the man is contrasted with the meme's confrontational text, which weaponizes his image. This reflects a broader pattern of using historical imagery to reinforce stereotypes or make inflammatory claims.",
