      "label": "Stereotype of Native Americans as either dignified or primitive",
      "description": "The meme relies on the real-world stereotype that Native Americans are either noble, wise, or 'other' — often portrayed as dignified in historical photos, which can be used to justify claims of superiority or to invoke a sense of 'authenticity.' This stereotype is often used to mask deeper issues of racism and cultural appropriation, and the meme weaponizes this image to make a confrontational statement.",
