    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_d279a706",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
      "label": "Native American identity as a shield is mapped onto the visual representation of the Native American man",
      "description": "The text 'bitch please i'm native american' explicitly asserts the speaker's Native American identity as a rhetorical shield against criticism. This textual claim is visually mapped onto the image of the Native American man, who is depicted in dignified, traditional attire. The visual material (the man) serves as the embodiment of the identity claimed in the text, creating an analogical mapping where the text's assertion is visually instantiated through the representation of the person. The man's dignified appearance reinforces the stereotype that Native Americans are noble or wise, which the text weaponizes to justify a dismissive or confrontational stance.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
